<section class="tm-ing"><div class="tm-w tm-ing-g"><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1786457342097-de7df8b3e7f8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=380&h=280&q=75" alt="five ears of corn with their husks" width="380" height="280" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Ma&iacute;z</figcaption></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1767032916116-2460bbd4a27d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=380&h=280&q=75" alt="market baskets full of vegetables" width="380" height="280" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Mercado</figcaption></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1779414518295-b03b6c60921b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=380&h=280&q=75" alt="grilled meat with salsas and tortillas" width="380" height="280" loading="lazy"><figcaption>La cena</figcaption></figure><p class="tm-ing-t rv">From the market to the steamer, a tamal is a whole day of cooking folded into one small parcel.</p></div></section>

<section class="tm-s tm-bt" id="batch"><div class="tm-w tm-bt-g"><div class="tm-card"><p class="tm-tag">Herramienta 1</p><h2 class="rv">Tamalada batch planner</h2><p class="tm-p">Tell us how many people are coming and how hungry they are. We work out how many tamales to make, and the masa, filling, husks and pot you will need.</p>
